    "body": "## What\nSwitch the `__shfl_xor_sync` masks in `deepseek_v4/main_norm_rope.cuh` from `0xffffffffu` to `warp::kFullMask`.\n\n## Why\n#45934 added `fused_k_norm_rope_flashmla_v41` (warp-per-token V4.1 K store). Its two shuffle loops pass a 32-bit mask, and ROCm's `amd_warp_sync_functions.h` statically requires a 64-bit mask, so the JIT module no longer builds on gfx950:\n\n```\namd_warp_sync_functions.h:307:62: error: static assertion failed due to requirement 'sizeof(unsigned int) == 8': The mask must be a 64-bit integer.\nmain_norm_rope.cuh:513:18: note: in instantiation of function template specialization '__shfl_xor_sync<unsigned int, float>'\n```\n\nThis breaks `test_v41_kv_store.py` in `stage-b-test-1-gpu-small-amd-mi35x` on main: https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39952723713/job/120410987523\n\n## Notes for the reviewer\n- `warp::kFullMask` is `uint32_t 0xffffffff` on CUDA and a 64-bit all-ones mask on ROCm, so CUDA codegen is unchanged. `fused_norm_rope_v2.cuh` already uses it for the same pattern.\n- The reduction logic needs no change on wave64: `kWarpThreads` is 32 on both platforms and every XOR mask is at most 16, so lanes never exchange across the two 32-lane halves of a wave.\n- The two Hadamard loops in the indexer Q kernels (lines 817 and 1034) had the same literal mask. They are not instantiated in the failing test, but I switched them too so the file is consistent.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `stage-b-test-1-gpu-small-amd-mi35x` (rocm10) on this commit, both partitions pass; `test_v41_kv_store.py` 8/8 OK: https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40067534793/job/120793883380\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40067564854](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40067564854)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40067564861](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40067564861)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40067564872](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40067564872)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\n",
